# Web and mobile stay in step

A feature prompt applies to both `apps/web` and `apps/mobile`. Check both before editing. Then add the missing side, or remove the feature from both.

## Check first

Search both trees and say what each side already has.

- Web: `apps/web/src/app/(app)/` and `apps/web/src/lib/nav.ts` (`NAV_BY_MODULE`, `PAGE_TITLES`).
- Mobile: `apps/mobile/app/`, `apps/mobile/src/screens/`, tab visibility in `apps/mobile/app/(app)/(tabs)/_layout.tsx`, and the More menu in `apps/mobile/src/screens/MoreScreen.tsx`.

Match on the user-facing behavior (route, screen, nav entry, and the API it calls), not only on a shared file name.

## Add or change

If either app lacks the feature, implement that side in the same change.

- Web: a route under `apps/web/src/app/(app)/<feature>/`, plus a `nav.ts` entry when it is a module.
- Mobile: a screen in `apps/mobile/src/screens/`, a route in `apps/mobile/app/`, and a tab or More row gated like the sibling features (role and module).
- Call the existing API. Share types from `@school-erp/shared`. Do not invent a second contract.

Example: a prompt to add a library loans page creates `apps/web/src/app/(app)/library/page.tsx` and a `LibraryScreen` plus `apps/mobile/app/(app)/library.tsx`. If the web page already exists, add only the mobile screen and menu entry.

## Remove

A remove prompt deletes the feature from both apps: page, screen, route, nav or More entry, and calls that exist only for it. Keep a shared API type when another feature still uses it.

## Leave these on the web unless the prompt names them

Academic setup, bulk student import, fee-structure editing, exam score entry, and turning an admission into a student. The proctored online-exam attempt stays in the browser.

## Done when

Both apps include the feature, or both no longer include it. The reply states the result for web and for mobile.
